# Original MIT Z80 diagnostic for Issue #73; installed at 0100h in a zero-filled
# system ROM. Each result captures F using PUSH AF / POP BC / LD A,C, stores it
# via DE at C100h, and advances DE. Expected bytes: 7D 91 39 7D 75 7D 75 7D.
# No proprietary firmware or debug interface; the captured bytes become glyph 0.
# DI; SP=F000; slots F0; expanded RAM subslots FF (ordinary RAM write on
# MSX1); (C000)=0, (C001)=FF; DE=C100.
f3 31 00 f0 3e f0 d3 a8 3e ff 32 ff ff 21 00 c0 36 00 23 36 ff 11 00 c1
# WZ=2800 survives immediate HL load; BIT 0 of zero with carry.
3a ff 27 21 00 c0 37 cb 46 f5 c1 79 12 13
# Full-word wrap gives WZ=0, opposite operand/address bits; BIT 7 of FF.
3a ff ff 21 01 c0 37 cb 7e f5 c1 79 12 13
# Register BIT still takes 3/5 from B, despite WZ=0.
3a ff ff 06 ff 37 cb 58 f5 c1 79 12 13
# Indexed displacement -128 gives address/WZ=2800, operand zero.
dd 21 80 28 37 dd cb 80 46 f5 c1 79 12 13
# Accumulator store wraps only low byte: 2800, then CPD borrows to 27FF.
3e 28 32 ff 40 21 00 c0 01 02 00 37 ed a9 21 00 c0 cb 46 f5 c1 79 12 13
# WZ=27FF, then CPI carries to 2800.
3a fe 27 21 00 c0 01 02 00 37 ed a1 21 00 c0 cb 46 f5 c1 79 12 13
# WZ=2800, then CPD borrows to 27FF.
3a ff 27 21 00 c0 01 02 00 37 ed a9 21 00 c0 cb 46 f5 c1 79 12 13
# Register-pair loads/increments, exchanges, CB RES and NOP preserve WZ.
3a ff 27 01 34 12 03 eb d9 21 00 c0 cb 86 00 11 07 c1 37 cb 7e f5 c1 79 12 13
# Graphics I: name table 1800, color table 2000, pattern table 0000.
3e 00 d3 99 3e 80 d3 99
3e 40 d3 99 3e 81 d3 99
3e 06 d3 99 3e 82 d3 99
3e 80 d3 99 3e 83 d3 99
3e 00 d3 99 3e 84 d3 99
3e 01 d3 99 3e 87 d3 99
# Glyph 0 foreground white/background black (F1).
3e 00 d3 99 3e 60 d3 99 3e f1 d3 98
# Copy the eight captured bytes from RAM to glyph 0 pattern via OTIR.
3e 00 d3 99 3e 40 d3 99 21 00 c1 01 98 08 ed b3
76
